{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787145477,"nonce":"CE1gTylwytEBcmxeepOhcwwuzQE=","message":"✅ **DONE — `4f5204f`, 88 files.** oto sends nothing unprompted.\n\nGone: the `notify.unacked_reminder` periodic and its worker, the sweep with its once-per-generation latch, the Reason, `notification_policies.unacked_reminder_after_s`, all five `orgs.settings` keys, the mention audience end to end, the Slack render path, the AC-52 scope gate, and the docs.\n\n⛔ **DELETED, NOT RETIRED — the owner's second ruling, and it reversed my first pass.** I had kept the Reason readable-but-unwritable on this ticket's own ⚠️ clause: `notifications.reason` has a thirteen-month horizon, so rows spelling it would have stopped decoding, and `a51a763` clause 5 is the standing warning against spending that concession twice. **The owner settled the premise instead: oto is unreleased and the database is being reset.** With no history to keep readable, `EventType`'s own test comes out the other way — *\"a value kept for a reader that cannot exist is not caution, it is a vocabulary entry the next person has to rule out.\"* No ghosts at launch.\n\nThat collapsed a lot: `Retired()`, `retiredReasons`, `SubscribableReasons()`, the writer refusal at the INSERT, and the wire-vs-storage ceiling split all went with it. **`MaxPolicyReasons`, `policies_reasons_ck` and all four wire `maxItems` now say 17**, sized from `len(AllReasons())` as the rule always said.\n\n⭐ **On the mention: removing it TIGHTENS the boundary rather than retreating from it.** `SCOPE-BOUNDARY §5.2` restricted the audience to usergroups and `!here`/`!channel` and dropped individual `\u003c@U…\u003e` mentions, because naming an individual names a RESPONDER and oto must never know who is on call (H-1, FR-1). With no mention surface at all there is nowhere left to cross that line. §G.9.1's one-stage clause is superseded by a **stronger** one — there are no stages, so there is no first stage for a second to follow — and `escalation` remains banned, because it was banned for dragging in rotas and ownership, which is true whether or not oto reminds anyone.\n\n⚠️ **And it closes by removal, not by evidence.** `2078a07` records that the `@`-mention path was **never once observed working** against a real workspace: Amendment 3 shipped it on Slack's documentation alone, and Amendment 4 is the standing proof that Slack's documentation can be half wrong. `slack-live-verification.md` step 8 was the step that would have tested it and was never run. ADR 0020 and the checklist now say that plainly rather than reading as a clean retirement.\n\n**Two migrations.** `00067` narrows `notifications_reason_ck` 18 → 17 and the policy ceiling with it, then strips the value from every `notification_policies.reasons` array and deletes the policies whose only reason it was — the strip is not optional and `00060` says so in the schema itself. `00068` drops the policy column with `policies_reminder_ck` and removes the five JSONB settings keys. The expand/contract exemption is re-verified rather than cited (`git tag` lists nothing), and the narrowing fails loudly rather than inventing a downlevel value.\n\n⭐ **`broadcast_refired` replaces `broadcast_unacked_reminder` in the card corpus, and the swap was not optional.** The reminder was the corpus's ONLY broadcast, and `reply_broadcast` is the one Slack parameter ADR 0020 Amendment 4 had to correct from a live workspace — deleting the reminder must not leave the mode uncaptured. The conformance probe moved with it: it wanted the word \"unacknowledged\", and a re-fire is self-sufficient on `Severity critical` and `firing again since`. The words changed; the rule did not.\n\n⚠️ **One guarantee is now corpus-wide rather than per-card.** `TestEveryBuilderCaptureIsSomethingBlockKitBuilderWillAccept` asserted every capture carries a mrkdwn `\u003c`, so the unicode-escape check above it could not pass vacuously. That held while the broadcast was the reminder, whose body carried a mention AND an \"open in oto\" link. A re-fire renders `:repeat: *Re-fired* — case #N` with neither. Demanding one per card would have meant inventing fixture content or dropping the guarantee.\n\n⚠️ **Filed separately, not fixed here:** the `refired` broadcast has no link back to oto. A broadcast is precisely the message that leaves the thread for the channel, read by people who have not been following — and it is now the one card with no way back.\n\n**Gate:** all eleven `ci` recipes individually. 9/11 green; the two reds are exactly the two pre-existing baselines (`lint-vocabulary` at 60, `TestNoStateHueInChrome` from `59c7def`) — one `--- FAIL` line in the whole suite. `test/integration` passed, so `TestEveryMigrationDownTo00028IsReversible` exercised **both** migrations in **both** directions with the pin at 68.","files":null}]}